@startuml
|Web Server|
start
:Detect Web hotspot;
:Send initialization request;

|Mediator|
:Receive initialization request;
:Obtain resource and access info;

|Service Registry|
:Provide resource and access info;

|Mediator|
:Obtain SLAs and policies;

|Policy Repository|
:Provide SLAs and policies;

|Mediator|
:Generate service requirements;
:Pass service requirements;

|Peering Agent|
:Discover external resources;
if (Preexisting peering arrangements?) then (yes)
  :Return preexisting arrangements;
else (no)
  :Negotiate with external PAs;
endif

|Mediator|
:Configure peering protocols;
:Advertise CDN configurations;
:Exchange content availability info;
:Support request redirection;

if (Sufficient resources acquired?) then (yes)
  :Deploy functional policies;
  :Administer peering arrangement;
  :Redirect portion of Web traffic;
  :Control content replication;
  :Exchange accounting information;
else (no)
  while (Any CDN interested in peering?) is (no)
    :Tune negotiated relationships;
    :Reconsider service requirements;
    |Peering Agent|
    :Negotiate with external PAs;
    |Mediator|
    if (Sufficient resources acquired?) then (yes)
      break
    endif
  endwhile (yes)
  :Deploy functional policies;
  :Administer peering arrangement;
  :Redirect portion of Web traffic;
  :Control content replication;
  :Exchange accounting information;
endif

if (Disband or re-arrange needed?) then (yes)
  :Disband peering arrangement;
else (no)
  :Re-arrange peering arrangement;
endif
stop
@enduml